 #:seon.task{:name "a-used-class-makes-a-row-host-bound"
             :plan "host-bound-callers marks a body host-bound when it uses a class outside sci.opts/default-classes (fn.clj:1049-1055, plus a Throwable/Error special case), although the agent interpreter now resolves every classpath class ({:classes {:allow :all}}, 2cae09887). 926 of 5,264 function entities on default were host-bound; the usual trigger is (java.util.Date.) in an error map. An agent-only function using (java.util.Date.) evaluates once, then refuses on every later call as 'host-bound ... load its source files'. Recommended (audit #1; fix-root-graph-panic option b, which needs a ruling on the branch interpretation cost): delete the java-class clause, re-derive the host-bound facts, then re-check whether adopt-then-test! and host-bound-declarations (about 80 lines) are still needed. Read `seon.fn/host-bound-callers`, `seon.sci.eval/install-row!`, `docs/research/agent-platform/agent-restrictions-and-rollback-2026-09-26.md`, `docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md`, `docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-root-graph-panic-2026-09-26.md` and `docs/seon/issues/an-agent-function-using-java-interop-is-host-bound-and-cannot-run-on-its-branch.md`."}
