 #:seon.task{:name "a-dependent-keeps-no-edge-to-a-callee-defined-after-it"
  :plan "(defn bad1 [x] (nosuch-fn x)) then (defn dep1 [x] (bad1 x)), then in a later pass a working bad1; and (declare later) (defn early [] (later)) (defn later [] 1): early and dep1 keep calls [clojure.core/defn] and gain no edge when the callee is defined. Related: seon.turn.batch/a-declared-var-call-stores-no-edge (the declare half). Correct: a caller's edge to a callee appears once the callee has an entity, without re-evaluating the caller. Proof: the last table row of the evidence (probe 7). Read `seon.fn/runtime-analysis-batch` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/failed-def-design.md`."}
