 #:seon.task{:name "gate-set-walks-the-whole-transitive-closure-to-select-two-levels"
             :plan "`seon.fn/gate-set` answers `seon.fn/closure-walk`'s `::selected` (the tests calling a seed or a direct caller) but `seon.fn/closure-walk` first walks every transitive caller level and derives `::affected` and `::tests` the caller drops. Measured at default fa92a2503 (agent ref-context, 2026-10-09, `seon.profile/measure` of `seon.ref/uses`): `seon.fs/attributes` (2 callers, 1 selected test) takes 22 ms, 40 MB and 209 reads (183 `seon.db/datoms`); `seon.db/pull` takes 98 ms, 192 MB and 1265 reads. `seon.ref/references` now calls it for every referenced program function in a task's block. Done when a selection-only caller walks two levels, so a leaf's cost follows its callers, measured on the same two seeds as a regression on reads."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-finding-without-a-row-throws-in-lint-entities"
             :plan "Appending `(deftest zz-d (clojure.test/are [x] (= x x) 1 2))` to test/seon/error_test.clj makes `seon.fn/analyze-entities` throw NullPointerException (`clojure.lang.RT/longCast` in `seon.fn/lint-entities`: a finding whose `:seon.fn.analyzer/row` is nil), so `my.program/write-branch!` of any test using `clojure.test/are` fails with an uncaught NPE instead of a write-back refusal (2026-10-10). Done when a positionless finding is file-scoped data and a test using `are` writes back. Read `seon.cluster.source/proven-file`."}
